@startuml
title Deployment Diagram - TravelWise (live, cloud-deployed state)

node "Vercel" {
  component "Static build\n(client, React)\ntravelwise-po1o.vercel.app" as Vite
}

node "Render" {
  component "Express API\n(server)\ntravelwise-server-6lp1.onrender.com" as Express
  component "Flask ML service\n(ml-service)\ntravelwise-ml-service.onrender.com" as Flask
  artifact "model.joblib" as Model
}

cloud "Supabase Cloud" {
  database "PostgreSQL" as PG
  component "Auth service" as Auth
}

Vite --> Express : HTTPS (VITE_API_URL)
Express --> Flask : HTTPS (ML_SERVICE_URL)
Flask --> Model : loaded at build time\n(from a GitHub release asset)
Express --> PG : REST (service role key)
Vite --> Auth : REST (publishable key)

note bottom
  Deployed per the target three-host split from
  Assignment 2 (React on Vercel; Node + Python
  on Render), each as its own independently
  deployable process, talking to the same managed
  Supabase Postgres + Auth used throughout
  development. See the traceability matrix (2.2)
  for the deployment requirement's status.
end note

@enduml
